From 2808b8d6e81367405ba73ef2f192549de3590db8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:07:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-62: a newer version installed -> one button to
 take it (0.62.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun: "你不能加個按鈕讓我reload嗎? 你這樣操作很複雜 就算我接受別人也沒辦法接受".
A VS Code window keeps the extension version it loaded; Ctrl+Shift+P ->
Developer: Reload Window was the only way, and nobody should have to know it.
- lib/update.js: the version VS Code registered in the extensions folder
  (extensions.json), compared as numbers (0.9 < 0.10)
- the extension looks every minute and whenever the window gets the focus;
  a newer one -> a status bar button "設計工具新版 v...: 按這裡更新" (warning
  colour), the 頁面 title says it, one message with 「現在更新」
- 重新載入視窗 button in the 頁面 title bar (always), and in the 元件 title
  bar / designer title bar while a newer version waits
- unsaved files survive a reload (hot exit); with files.hotExit off it asks
  to save first
- a copy run from the source tree finds nothing (no extensions folder)
- README / CHEATSHEET / CHANGELOG: the button; from before 0.62 a window has
  to be closed and opened once

Tests: lib (versions, newest registered, unreadable = null), smoke (button,
title, one message, reload, the hotExit question, gone when nothing newer),
real VS Code (the same against a temp extensions folder; the reload itself
is not run). lib 137/0, smoke 137/0, probe + panels pass, real VS Code 134/0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
